Cropping Operation

The input video resolution is:

Input: 1920×1080
Output: 1280×720

The crop window is centered within the input frame.

        1920 pixels
┌───────────────────────────────┐
│                               │
│      ┌─────────────────┐      │
│      │                 │      │
│      │    1280×720     │      │
│      │   Crop Region   │      │
│      │                 │      │
│      └─────────────────┘      │
│                               │
└───────────────────────────────┘
          1080 lines
AXI4-Stream Handling

The cropper monitors the incoming pixel stream and forwards only pixels belonging to the configured crop window.

The output stream maintains the required AXI4-Stream video signaling, including:

TVALID
TREADY
TDATA
TUSER
TLAST

TUSER is regenerated for the beginning of the cropped output frame, while TLAST identifies the end of each output video line.

Verification

The cropper was verified using a Verilog simulation testbench.

Verification focused on:

Crop-window correctness
Pixel pass-through behavior
Output frame boundaries
TUSER alignment
TLAST alignment
AXI4-Stream handshake behavior
Waveform-level timing analysis
Integration

The custom cropper was integrated into the Zybo Z7-10 video pipeline and connected with AXI VDMA for DDR frame buffering.

The cropped 1280×720 frames were subsequently processed by the VPSS Scaler Only subsystem for conversion back to 1920×1080 before HDMI display.

